note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note om/hive-task/drive.om: the checks of the hive forge task rules (issue #925, DRA-288, DRA-162).
note Build with the pinned omc: omc < om/hive-task/drive.om > drive
note Run: drive MODE RULES COCKPIT SCRATCH DIR OMC MAIN
note   MODE     cases, http, table or migrate
note   RULES    om/hive-task/task.om compiled by the pinned omc
note   COCKPIT  the spark-cockpit-rs binary under test (the branch build, or main's as the control)
note   SCRATCH  an existing empty directory; every database, log and file of the run is made there
note   DIR      om/hive-task (cases.tsv and task.om are read from it)
note   OMC      the pinned omc; mode table rebuilds mutants of task.om with it
note   MAIN     spark-cockpit-rs built from main; mode migrate opens main's database with COCKPIT
note Modes:
note   cases    runs RULES once per line of cases.tsv and compares stdout and exit status.
note   http     starts COCKPIT on an ephemeral loopback port with a scratch database and drives
note            /api/hive/forge/* over HTTP: T1 to T3, stale attempts, expired leases, generation
note            exhaustion, ttl range (400 invalid), bad JSON bodies (400 invalid), artifact
note            binding, a held write lock, 400 claim races between two cockpit processes sharing
note            one database file, command-id replay (same body, no second change, 409
note            command_conflict on a different payload, across both processes and under a race),
note            and a commit that cannot complete (the cockpit must not answer 200 for it).
note   table    seeds every combination of state, generation, fence, artifact, verdict, lease and
note            ttl for each operation, applies it through the API, and checks that RULES predicts
note            each outcome and next state; op 7 does the same for command ids (prior record,
note            same or different payload, id length and characters, task state); then shows
note            that mutants of task.om fail the checks.
note   migrate  makes a database with MAIN, opens it with COCKPIT and checks the migration.
note Output: one line per check, "PASS name ..." or "FAIL name ...", then a SUMMARY line. Exit 0
note only when nothing failed.
note Host programs on this test path only, never shipped: /usr/bin/sqlite3 (3.45.1) seeds rows the
note API cannot create (any status, a generation near 2^53, an expired lease), holds a write lock
note for the busy case and a read lock on a rollback-journal database for the commit case.
note /usr/bin/env is a temporary bridge in cockexec, because execprog starts a program with an
note empty environment.
om2
